special_abilities:
  - name: "Lemurian R.C.C. Abilities"
    description: "The Birdman keeps everything the Lemurian race gives (see the Lemurian racial description). As restated on printed 67: Life Sense - 25 foot (7.6 m) radius plus 5 feet (1.5 m) per level, with a 20% +5% per level chance to locate, track or find a specific kind of animal or plant, +5% underwater. Empathy with Animals - an automatic affinity with animals of all kinds other than monsters, predators and sentient creatures. Ley Line Powers - heals and recovers P.P.E. at twice a normal human''s rate on a ley line or at a stone pyramid, and swims 25% faster along ley lines. Natural Abilities, and Pets and Familiars, as all Lemurians; Birdmen who keep pets, Familiars or riding animals usually choose birds and other fliers. Ultrasonic Communication - hears and makes high frequency sounds to communicate, out to 2,000 feet (610 m) underwater and 400 feet (122 m) on the surface or in the air."
  - name: "Communicate with and Control Moai"
    description: "Exclusive to Birdmen. A natural link to the Moai Stone Guardians lets the Birdman feel when one reacts to supernatural evil: he knows at once where the threat is, roughly what it is, and whether the danger is low, medium or high. He also knows when a Moai is under attack, how many enemies it faces and exactly where it is. While fighting alongside a Moai the link adds +1 on Perception Rolls, +1 on initiative and +2 to automatic dodge, on top of the O.C.C. bonuses. Only a select handful of trusted, combat-proven Birdmen are given the secret words that activate and pilot a Moai - a rare honor, though granted to more Birdmen than to any other Lemurian fighting class (G.M.''s call; see the Moai under Easter Island)."
  - name: "Ride the Moai"
    description: "The Birdman can fly underwater as well as in the air, to a maximum depth of two miles (3.2 km). Perched on the top or sides of a Moai''s head and holding on, he is coated in a thin crust of hardened lava and becomes a temporary part of the Stone Guardian, and can then be carried as an observer as deep as 6 miles (9.6 km). While attached he can take no action of his own, and he cannot let go until the Moai is back at two miles (3.2 km) or shallower - disengaging any deeper means being crushed by the pressure."
  - name: "Manutara Companion"
    description: "The Birdman is bonded to a manutara, a Sooty Tern, which once fully grown serves as his companion and Familiar. A seagull or almost any other aquatic bird may be substituted, but the tern is the tradition. Sooty Tern: 13 to 14.2 inches (33 to 36 cm) long with a 32.3 to 37 inch (82 to 94 cm) wingspan. Speed 8 on dry land, 12 in the water, 55 flying (35 mph/56 km). Hit Points 1D8+2, S.D.C. 2D6+2, no A.R., P.P.E. 2D4+1. Flies, Swim 90%, depth tolerance 10 feet (3 m), keen hawk-like vision and exceptional endurance (known to stay out at sea for 3-10 years at a time). +2 to save vs toxins and magic, and takes half damage from cold. Two attacks per melee; bite or peck 1D4 S.D.C., claws 1D4 S.D.C. The bird is +2 on Perception Rolls, +1 on initiative, +2 to strike and +5 to dodge."
  - name: "Birdman O.C.C. Bonuses"
    description: "+6D6 S.D.C., +1 on Perception Rolls, +2 to automatic dodge (dodging does not use up a melee attack), +2 to save vs possession, +1 to save vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 4, 8, 12 and 15, and +1 to save vs magic at levels 3, 8 and 12. All of these are in the stored bonuses."
restrictions:
  - "Race: so far every Birdman is a Lemurian of the Tangata Manu clan (printed 67 spells it Tangatu Manu)."
  - "Alignment: usually Principled or Scrupulous. Not a hard limit."
  - "Psionics: standard as per all Lemurians - see the Lemurian racial description. The O.C.C. adds none, so no psionics block is stored here."
  - "Cybernetics: none. Lemurians have no interest in bionics, not even Bio-Systems."
  - "Money: a monthly salary of 2,000 credits or trade goods, double for squadron leaders; starts with one month''s pay."
  - "Starting gear also includes one weapon for every W.P. (with 3 extra clips where applicable; these may be Biomancy weapons), 1D4+1 symbiotes of choice, a few sets of clothes and some personal items. Birdmen have access to all Bio-Skins and may be issued extra weapons, gear or symbiotes for special missions."
  - "Birdmen may be assigned as aerial troops on any but the smallest Lemurian stone vehicles and submarines."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria printed 66-68 (cache p067-p069). The entry
    starts under the heading "Lemurian Men-At-Arms O.C.C.s" on printed 66 and
    ends at its Money paragraph on printed 68, above the Oceanic Guardsman
    heading. The skills, equipment, cybernetics and money are all on printed
    68. Every number was read off renders of printed 67 and 68.
  - men_of_arms true and occ_group men-of-arms: read off the section heading
    "Lemurian Men-At-Arms O.C.C.s" (printed 66). The book prints no S.D.C.
    base for the class, only "+6D6 S.D.C.", stored as a pool bonus.
  - xp_table: the "Birdman & Junk Crab" ladder on the Experience Tables,
    printed 86, read off a render; lower bounds.
  - Save vs magic +1 at levels 3, 8 and 12 is stored on both spell_magic and
    ritual_magic. Save vs Horror Factor +1 at levels 2, 4, 8, 12 and 15.
  - The Moai link bonuses (+1 Perception, +1 initiative, +2 automatic dodge
    when fighting together with a Moai) are conditional and stay in the
    ability''s prose.
  - "Skills Known by All Lemurians" are printed inside the O.C.C. with this
    class''s own figures and stored as occ_skills. Language: Lemurian and
    Oceanic at 98% with no per-level figure printed -> per_level 1, the
    native-speaker rate the skill descriptions print on printed 55. Literacy:
    Lemurian (85% +2%) is granted by name at those figures. The O.C.C. Skills line Language: Oceanic (+20%) would be 70%
    and is below the 98% already printed, so one Oceanic entry at 98 is
    stored and the +20% is in its note.
  - Skills renamed to the catalog: Lore: Faeries and Creatures of Magic ->
    Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic (25+20); Lore: Demons and Monsters ->
    Lore: Demons & Monsters (25+20); Tracking -> Tracking (people) (25+15);
    Jet Pack -> Jet Packs; Hand to Hand: Kapu Kuialua -> Hand to Hand: Demon
    Combat. Other bases: Climbing 40+5, Intelligence 32+10, Land Navigation
    36+15, Navigation 40+20, Prowl 25+10, Wilderness Survival 30+15.
  - W.P. Ancient: one of choice is a pick across Weapon Proficiencies with
    the limit in its note; the catalog does not mark a W.P. ancient or modern.
  - AQUATIC: ANY (+5%). The catalog has no Aquatic category. The book''s
    Aquatic Skills list (printed 54) is seventeen skills, held under six
    catalog categories. Stored as one related-skills entry named Aquatic
    whose only list names fourteen of them at +5%. Left out: Language:
    Lemurian and Language: Oceanic (O.C.C. skills here) and Horsemanship:
    Serpent Hunter (the Serpent Hunter''s own). Track & Hunt Sea Animals and
    Undersea & Sea Survival are also Wilderness rows, and Wilderness: Any
    prints +10%; named in the Aquatic entry they score its +5%, not +10%.
  - Communication +5% list: Creative Writing, Language and Literacy rows are
    filed under Technical in the catalog and get Technical''s own +5%.
  - Pilot: "excluding military, power armor and robots" is stored as the
    Military prefix, the Robot Combat prefix and Robots & Power Armor. Air
    Assault Armor, Combat Pod and Flight System Combat are left selectable.
  - Equipment: "two Bio-Construct Weapons" is a pick of two from every
    Lemurian weapon row (printed 131-136) less the two Serpent Bio-Weapons,
    since the book does not list which. "1D4+1 symbiotes of choice" is a pick of two (the lowest roll)
    from the eight symbiote rows, with the roll in the note. "A few sets of
    clothes" is one clothing row. One weapon per W.P. with 3 extra clips and
    the personal items are prose.
  - starting_money 2000: "starts off with one month''s pay" at a monthly
    salary of 2,000 credits. The squadron leader''s double pay is prose.
  - Race: no race_restrictions block. "So far, all Birdmen are Lemurians"
    is prose in restrictions.
  - The Lemurian R.C.C. abilities restated on printed 67 are one prose
    ability. Psionics "standard as per all Lemurians" is the race''s and not
    stored here.
---

# Birdman Warrior

## Lore

The Birdmen are the oldest of Lemuria''s warrior orders, older than the fall of Atlantis. They began as the Tangata Manu, a clan on Easter Island that revered birds and birds of prey, and for close to a thousand years they were the only armed protectors Lemuria had. The other fighting orders were raised only after the return to Rifts Earth.

An initiate once had to climb down the cliffs of Rapa Nui, swim through shark-filled water to the islet of Motu Nui and carry back a Sooty Tern''s egg without needing rescue. He raised the chick himself, and when both had come of age the bird became his companion and a clan Biomancer grew a suit of winged Avian Bio-Armor for him alone. Before taking a place in the order he spent a year as the sole guardian of a small village, answerable for everything that happened to it - a lesson in humility the order still values.

Today they are Lemuria''s air force in all but name, more at ease in the sky than beneath the waves, and still based on Easter Island. They are peacekeepers first, expected to settle a quarrel with words before weapons, and they started the Lemurian tradition of the warrior who is also a poet and a thinker.

## GM Notes

Birdmen share a bond with the Moai Stone Guardians and sense what the statues sense. Only the most trusted are taught the words that wake and steer one; that is a reward to hand out in play, not something a new character starts with. The best of the order fight the worst supernatural threats side by side with the Moai.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'birdman-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'birdman-warrior';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-birdman-warrior-class.sql');
